{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game","id":555110,"title":"How would you handle species Hybridization in game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-14T19:26:15-07:00","id":555110,"title":"How would you handle species Hybridization in game?","content":"So I was reading an article recently <a href=\"http://news.nationalgeographic.com/news/2011/11/111107-hybrids-coyotes-wolf-virginia-dna-animals-science/\" target=\"_blank\">here.</a> I read other articles on this as well, but this was the first I could find to link.<br /> In any case, the article is about the increasing occurrence of coyotes mating with wolves. More and more coyotes, along the east coast in particular, are turning up with wolf DNA. It seems to be a matter of adaption through hybridization.<br /> Some of the &quot;Coywolves&quot; also have domestic dog DNA in them. One study showed that the new hybrid species that is expanding eastward is (roughly) 64% coyote, 13% western gray wolf, 13% eastern wolf species and the remaining 10% were domestic dog (presumably feral). There are other percentages for different groups that have been studied as well, this was just the one that pertained most directly to the article I was reading. <br /> <br /> So I was wondering what this would mean for the world of W:tA. How do you think spirits would deal with this, and how do you think this would affect Garou and Nuwisha? Obviously with coyotes showing up with wolf DNA, there are also wolves showing up with coyote DNA.<br /> <br /> <br /> The other WoD species this affects is the Gurahl, but to a much lesser extent since their Tribes don't divide clearly by bear species. There are 3 confirmed cases in the wild of polar bear/grizzly bear hybrids. For the Gurahl though, tribe is more a matter of which tribe needs numbers and is completely determined by spiritual factors, from what I remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:31:31-07:00","id":555156,"title":"","content":"The normal answer is that it's about spirit, not genetics, so I'm going to work on the assumption we're just doing the one-shifter type, breed of the mother but kin to both thing for this particular answer.<br /> <br /> It would depend on the spirit, but any sort of &quot;middle ground&quot; critter would probably be more likely to be well received by spirits that treat with both parents. So, for example the Garou + Nuwisha offspring, assuming it became a Garou shifter, might be better able to communicate with trickster spirits, spirits of umbral travle and the deeper umbral broods regardless of its Auspice. A Nuwisha shifter of the same parents might be better able to communicate with spirits of Garou ancestry, since Nuwisha can basically already get their paws on anything else already anyway.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, keeping with the basic rule of &quot;breed of the mother&quot; sorting out the phenotype and genotype issues, the most important thing is role. What is their role for Gaia? Garou and Nuwisha have vastly different duties in practice, as a Shifter type, before we even get to breaking it down into their &quot;Auspices&quot; and more specialized aspects.<br /> <br /> Ligers (and I guess Tiglions, but no one talks about them anyway) are another interesting example of the cross breeding. Would you use Simba yava or Khan yava? One of each? Would spirits or Jamak that have relations with those specific breeds consider a Liger Bastet as part of both families, outcast to both, or simply one or the other? I think it's an interesting element to include in Chronicles (provided it isn't simply to cheese a broader range of Gifts), but ultimately highly circumstantial, case by case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T22:47:33-07:00","id":555324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=555156#post555156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ligers (and I guess Tiglions, but no one talks about them anyway) are another interesting example of the cross breeding. Would you use Simba yava or Khan yava? One of each? Would spirits or Jamak that have relations with those specific breeds consider a Liger Bastet as part of both families, outcast to both, or simply one or the other? I think it's an interesting element to include in Chronicles (provided it isn't simply to cheese a broader range of Gifts), but ultimately highly circumstantial, case by case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as a note for the situation, a lion fathering offspring will likely have 'Huge Size, while a lion mothering offspring will have 'Small Size'. This is due to an enzyme the lion produces in order for his offspring to be larger than other lions in the pride, while the females produce a counter-enzyme for it to keep sizes reasonable. It developed due to the fact that multiple males may share females. I don't recall if Cheetahs have a similar issue, but I don't think so, as they aren't built for size and power.<br /> <br /> But that being said, for Bastet, flip a coin. I wouldn't make a 'mixed Tribe' Bastet any more than I would a 'mixed Auspice' Garou. They are prone to physical problems, but it isn't absolute. Possible Deformity flaws, but not required.<br /> <br /> They would probably have some social flaws, to show the mistrust their tribe would have in such a case. They would likely have to push for appropriate Gifts and Rites to 'go it alone', and attending a Taghairm would likely be mixed tribe events. (Such as the Colorado one in the Breedbook.)<br /> <br /> One big example: Black Tooth. While being told that his fur color was the result of a deal with Cahlash (the Wyrm), it was more likely that he just had a black Leopard (or Jaguar) mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T23:33:43-07:00","id":555358,"title":"","content":"Bastet can probably handle it almost like Garou with conflicting heritage, except that instead of a rite of passage and acceptance by a totem, it's whichever kuasha chooses to entrust the Yava with the prospective tekmet. If taken in by a Khan mentor and taught the Khan yava, a liger-born Bastet is Khan.<br /> <br /> Now, li-tigons, ti-ligers, li-ligers, and ti-tigons, and further crosses, those are headaches... (^VVVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T23:48:24-07:00","id":555363,"title":"","content":"So even before the true blooded shifter thing, do you think that a hybrid animal would count as kin to both? or is it one or the other or neither?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=555156#post555156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The normal answer is that it's about spirit, not genetics, so I'm going to work on the assumption we're just doing the one-shifter type, breed of the mother but kin to both thing for this particular answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree that situations that come up in Werewolf are more about spirit than genetics. Even still, this is an interesting occurrence that I felt might end up with a more fleshed out answer. This isn't about a single individual (like a Liger/Tiglion) but about a whole species. The genetic testing was done on over 400 individuals, so it's fairly widespread. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=555156#post555156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In my opinion, keeping with the basic rule of &quot;breed of the mother&quot; sorting out the phenotype and genotype issues, the most important thing is role. What is their role for Gaia? Garou and Nuwisha have vastly different duties in practice, as a Shifter type, before we even get to breaking it down into their &quot;Auspices&quot; and more specialized aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what I said above: breed of the mother may or may not end up being the answer since a whole species is changing. Will the resultant hybrid species be able to breed with (be kinfolk to) both, and maybe not be able to breed true with either?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=555156#post555156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ligers (and I guess Tiglions, but no one talks about them anyway) are another interesting example of the cross breeding. Would you use Simba yava or Khan yava? One of each? Would spirits or Jamak that have relations with those specific breeds consider a Liger Bastet as part of both families, outcast to both, or simply one or the other? I think it's an interesting element to include in Chronicles (provided it isn't simply to cheese a broader range of Gifts), but ultimately highly circumstantial, case by case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liger/Tiglions are a much more common example I didn't think of for some reason. The initial article I had read was talking about how these new hybrid species might end up adapting and surviving while the parent species cannot due to changing circumstances. Aside from the issues in the real world, I was thinking about what this might mean for the World of Darkness. What sort of stories could be told using this information.<br /> I prefer the idea of this being worked into a story as naturally occurring, and dealing with possible benefits. But a darker story could also have the species being altered on purpose to make them unable to breed with their respective Fera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=555324#post555324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, as a note for the situation, a lion fathering offspring will likely have 'Huge Size, while a lion mothering offspring will have 'Small Size'. This is due to an enzyme the lion produces in order for his offspring to be larger than other lions in the pride, while the females produce a counter-enzyme for it to keep sizes reasonable. It developed due to the fact that multiple males may share females. I don't recall if Cheetahs have a similar issue, but I don't think so, as they aren't built for size and power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting to know. Thanks for the information.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=555324#post555324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But that being said, for Bastet, flip a coin. I wouldn't make a 'mixed Tribe' Bastet any more than I would a 'mixed Auspice' Garou. They are prone to physical problems, but it isn't absolute. Possible Deformity flaws, but not required.<br /> <br /> They would probably have some social flaws, to show the mistrust their tribe would have in such a case. They would likely have to push for appropriate Gifts and Rites to 'go it alone', and attending a Taghairm would likely be mixed tribe events. (Such as the Colorado one in the Breedbook.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Bastet would actually be more understanding of the situation, and the resulting Hybrid cat would be expected to go it alone anyways since that's the Bastet's way (mostly). At least in this case, while I think breed would be an issue, it might not be quite as bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=555324#post555324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One big example: Black Tooth. While being told that his fur color was the result of a deal with Cahlash (the Wyrm), it was more likely that he just had a black Leopard (or Jaguar) mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this brings up an interesting related question. If you accept that Pure Breed can come and go generation to generation dependent on the deeds of individuals (which is arguable either way), what do you think Black-Tooth's kids pure breed would be? If his parent was a Panther (maybe), then he should have 0 Pure Breed. But his deeds, as morally questionable as they were, were certainly the stuff of Legend which would be carried on in any surviving offspring.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T00:13:25-07:00","id":555368,"title":"","content":"If the hybrid was able to reproduce, my default answer would be Kin To Both. Whether or not they accept it as Kin would be another story, but it would theoretically carry the potential for a Shifter of either breed to happen in its line.<br /> <br /> You get into a whole host of odd philosophical questions with it too, in regards to the roles. Like, say these Wolf+Coyote hybrids established a healthy breeding population, and then they were no longer able to produce viable (healthy, fertile) offspring with either wolves or coyotes, but only each other. At that point they are effectively something else entirely. If they produce Shifters that are these hybrids, what is even their place? Their mandated role? Are they sacred tricksters and teachers, or are they warriors? Is such a thing natural, a process of every-evolving nature and Wyld? Is their having Shifters an indication of Gaia's blessing, or is it something twisted and perverse, like what is being seen with the shapeshifters created by Pentex?<br /> <br /> I could see something like this being a really intriguing off-the-beaten-path seed for a Chronicle with inquisitive, thoughtful players. I could see using hybridization in a number of ways, from adding to roles to consolidating them; to adapt to survive what may happen after the Apocalypse (if there is to be an &quot;after&quot; in a given way it might be run, be it the actual end of the world, or just an end of a cycle and the beginning of a new one), or to better weather it in the present. Perhaps the Nuwisha and Garou are both meant to be killed off, and it is the hybrid Wolfyotes that would survive to replace both! Perhaps they are &quot;reinforcements&quot;. Lots of possibilities. But whatever the case, the Garou probably wouldn't take it well, if their history has shown us any RP notes. Haha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":2810,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","user":"Yakecen-Sings","date":". 06-15-2015, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T01:23:45-07:00","id":555393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=555368#post555368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get into a whole host of odd philosophical questions with it too, in regards to the roles. Like, say these Wolf+Coyote hybrids established a healthy breeding population, and then they were no longer able to produce viable (healthy, fertile) offspring with either wolves or coyotes, but only each other. At that point they are effectively something else entirely. If they produce Shifters that are these hybrids, what is even their place? Their mandated role? Are they sacred tricksters and teachers, or are they warriors? Is such a thing natural, a process of every-evolving nature and Wyld? Is their having Shifters an indication of Gaia's blessing, or is it something twisted and perverse, like what is being seen with the shapeshifters created by Pentex?</div> </div> </div> </div>These are the kind of thoughts I was thinking. Given that there were over 400 tested subjects, it seems that it's a stable breeding population. I don't think there is any chance of them no longer being able to breed with the &quot;parent&quot; species, since the wolves and coyotes were close enough to breed after splitting from each other so long ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=555368#post555368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I could see something like this being a really intriguing off-the-beaten-path seed for a Chronicle with inquisitive, thoughtful players. I could see using hybridization in a number of ways, from adding to roles to consolidating them; to adapt to survive what may happen after the Apocalypse (if there is to be an &quot;after&quot; in a given way it might be run, be it the actual end of the world, or just an end of a cycle and the beginning of a new one), or to better weather it in the present. Perhaps the Nuwisha and Garou are both meant to be killed off, and it is the hybrid Wolfyotes that would survive to replace both! Perhaps they are &quot;reinforcements&quot;. Lots of possibilities. But whatever the case, the Garou probably wouldn't take it well, if their history has shown us any RP notes. Haha.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough, on the response of the Garou. It seems the interbreeding started somewhere around the great lakes, and the hybrids have slowly been expanding eastward for the last 60-70 years. There is a growing population in Virginia which is where the 400+ eastern coyote-wolf hybrid samples were taken.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T01:35:54-07:00","id":555399,"title":"","content":"With current situation, that is a population (one sadly larger than the Mexican wolf, along with a few other subspecies) that is able to breed with both, I'd stick with Kin To Both and the potential for either Nuwisha or Garou on some kind of random die roll, maybe favoring one or the other based on whatever circumstances might want to be considered. The social dynamics would be rough, I think, but interesting. Oh man, and breeding rights, disputes over Tribe, kinfolk, or Pure Breed, let alone ancestral things! In my opinion, as long as the hybrid was respectful as they ought to be, though, the spirits would get on with them just as well. Maybe confusion here and there. But with Ancestor spirits in particular, it's still their descendent, and as long as they continue to live honorably (in accordance with whatever that means in the situation) then hey. Sure they look odd, but family's family.<br /> <br /> Unifier type characters might even actively pursue them as a new source of &quot;lupus&quot; kinfolk. Maybe it's the Wyld or Gaia's way of offering a reprieve, after all, to have cousins mingle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:23:32-07:00","id":555457,"title":"","content":"They'd be kin to both, and they could become either. If two kin like that hooked up, they'd have a minor chance to produce a Nuwisha or a Garou, and if a kin slept with a shifter... well, then the shifter's breed would be the one that would decide which way the offspring went.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T05:23:47-07:00","id":555510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=555363#post555363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think Bastet would actually be more understanding of the situation, and the resulting Hybrid cat would be expected to go it alone anyways since that's the Bastet's way (mostly). At least in this case, while I think breed would be an issue, it might not be quite as bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> So this brings up an interesting related question. If you accept that Pure Breed can come and go generation to generation dependent on the deeds of individuals (which is arguable either way), what do you think Black-Tooth's kids pure breed would be? If his parent was a Panther (maybe), then he should have 0 Pure Breed. But his deeds, as morally questionable as they were, were certainly the stuff of Legend which would be carried on in any surviving offspring.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Noteriety flaw would be perfect for both situations. Pure Breed would balance it out for one of BT's kids, were he to have any.<br /> <br /> I think they would be happy about teaching Bastet Gifts, or Breed Gifts. But the nagging question of 'are you really my Tribe' would crop up for Tribal Gifts (or Rites, if there are any.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T06:42:07-07:00","id":555581,"title":"","content":"Way back on Shadownessence, <b>Chris Campbell</b> weighed in on Bastet hybrids on two occasions. This is what he had to say:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In game terms, the matter is simple -- the critter winds up looking like the Bastet parent, and if it changes it belongs said parent's tribe. If the other parent is kin to another Bastet tribe the cub has the normal chance to be kin to said tribe. And if it's two Bastet doing the mating, the progeny looks like a metis from one parent or the other (and I guess it'd be possible to put Simba and Khan in the same litter if you really really want to). </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On-topic, my two cents: it's a metis of the mother's tribe. Play with metis deformities (huge size, etc) as you like. </div> </div> </div>But also:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, I've gone on record in the past saying that IMO the Bastet should be a bunch of different Breeds (same with most of the other Fera tribes). But that way lies extensive rewrites of the setting and added work for the ST, so buyer be warned. </div> </div> </div>See the full discussions here:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.shadownesssence.com/forum/index.php?/topic/20281-hercules-the-liger/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.shadownesssence.com/forum/index.php?/topic/20281-hercules-the-liger/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.shadownesssence.com/forum/index.php?/topic/20281-hercules-the-liger/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.shadownesssence.com/forum/index.php?/topic/20281-hercules-the-liger/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.shadownesssence.com/forum/index.php?/topic/25369-ligers-tigons-and-others-alike/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.shadownesssence.com/forum/index.php?/topic/25369-ligers-tigons-and-others-alike/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.shadownesssence.com/forum/index.php?/topic/25369-ligers-tigons-and-others-alike/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.shadownesssence.com/forum/index.php?/topic/25369-ligers-tigons-and-others-alike/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T11:41:05-07:00","id":555878,"title":"","content":"Yeah, he said similar things on the mailing list. (Lists? I can't remember if it was over Oracle or the White Wolf one.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T16:49:10-07:00","id":556220,"title":"","content":"A player of mine and I covered this topic once. We had her related to the Shadow Lords and was the result of her Nuwisha fathers sense of humor (her family had a high pure breed rating and he was looking to mess things up). We gave her the Nuwisha merit &quot;large&quot; from its breed book. The only benefit is you get an extra social die when dealing with garou, and you're larger than other Nuwisha in your other forms passing as garou easier. We took that to show her Coywolf heritage. She was still a Nuwisha but with a small merit spin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T16:51:35-07:00","id":556222,"title":"","content":"My player who has an environmental science degree said that the black fur color that pops up sometimes in coyotes has been traced to wolves, which then was traced back to dogs....anyone know anything about this? Could be fun at the Shadow Lord and Black Furies expense!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:17:02-07:00","id":556332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=556220#post556220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A player of mine and I covered this topic once. We had her related to the Shadow Lords and was the result of her Nuwisha fathers sense of humor (her family had a high pure breed rating and he was looking to mess things up). We gave her the Nuwisha merit &quot;large&quot; from its breed book. The only benefit is you get an extra social die when dealing with garou, and you're larger than other Nuwisha in your other forms passing as garou easier. We took that to show her Coywolf heritage. She was still a Nuwisha but with a small merit spin.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is a way to handle it (just giving the character the large Merit), it seems the simplest route, and the least interesting story-wise. This is a changing/adaption of a species to possibly fill the role left vacant after most of the wolf population on the east coast have died out. The newer hybrid have been working together to take down deer, which is something coyotes normally would have trouble with. They can't completely fill the role the wolves did, insomuch as the larger prey (moose and stags) are still beyond them. But it is an interesting development nonetheless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=556222#post556222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My player who has an environmental science degree said that the black fur color that pops up sometimes in coyotes has been traced to wolves, which then was traced back to dogs....anyone know anything about this? Could be fun at the Shadow Lord and Black Furies expense!</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing I could find on this is that coyotes at higher elevations tend to have the darker fur coats. It is theorized that it may be due to wolf hybridization, but DNA tests would be needed to confirm this, and it doesn't look like they've actually been done/documented yet.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T19:47:21-07:00","id":556400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=556332#post556332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that is a way to handle it (just giving the character the large Merit), it seems the simplest route, and the least interesting story-wise. This is a changing/adaption of a species to possibly fill the role left vacant after most of the wolf population on the east coast have died out. The newer hybrid have been working together to take down deer, which is something coyotes normally would have trouble with. They can't completely fill the role the wolves did, insomuch as the larger prey (moose and stags) are still beyond them. But it is an interesting development nonetheless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For us it wasn't about evolution, so much as it was about that individual character. She lived her life raised by Shadow Lords, and then upon her first change...SURPRISE NO YOU'RE NOT A WEREWOLF!!!! as long lost dad you didn't know was dad leaps out of the bathroom mirror....it was about hiding what she was from her family, and the terror of what would happen if her Shadow Lord family found out what she was. She went missing for years learning how to be a nuwisha and didn't return back until after she could hide her true nature from detection (what's the gift? Sheep's Clothing? it was Rank 2...don't have my Nuwisha book on me).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T10:02:08-07:00","id":672145,"title":"","content":"Sorry to revive a dead thread, but I was reading about the Debased a little while back, which are wolf/dog hybrids, brought about by the Rite of Adaptation. It reads in one section: &quot;Garou were never meant to breed with dogs, and the Rite of Adaptation is no way around that. Debased aren't &quot;weredogs,&quot; a blending of canine, man, and spirit in a gestalt whole. Mutts are unnatural hybrids of werewolves and domestic canines, conflicting spirits and genetics in a twisted, weak creature. All Debased characters have one deformity, known as a debasement, chosen from the list of Metis deformities.&quot; (page 20.) Also, if the character is Metis, the deformities do stack. (If you're curious about the Rite, the book doesn't give much on it in terms of origin. It states it was left open on purpose.)<br /> <br /> So, my best guess is that, while normal wolves and coyotes can breed and produce viable offspring, Garou and Nuwisha will only end up being the mother's race, unless a Rite, such as the one stated above, is used. In addition, according to the book, cross-breeding with dogs is seen as corrupting the bloodline, so I'd imagine the same holds true for breeding with coyotes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7983-shadow-of-twilight","name":"Shadow of Twilight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T15:04:21-07:00","id":672389,"title":"","content":"I can't tell from what you're posting but, you do know the Debased are just a fan creation right? not cannon in anyway...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T16:42:25-07:00","id":672478,"title":"","content":"While the thread is already up: I believe it was one of the Urrah tribebooks or perhaps book of the city that established that something that isn't at least 9/10 wolf has no chance of being a Garou. That obviously has no bearing on human kinfolk of different species, in which case I'd say: Kin to both, but a shifter only gets &quot;active&quot; genetic traits from their own species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T20:44:36-07:00","id":672833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=672478#post672478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the thread is already up: I believe it was one of the Urrah tribebooks or perhaps book of the city that established that something that isn't at least 9/10 wolf has no chance of being a Garou. That obviously has no bearing on human kinfolk of different species, in which case I'd say: Kin to both, but a shifter only gets &quot;active&quot; genetic traits from their own species.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this was in the Bone Gnawer tribe book, but it specifically referred to Garou and dogs. And it had to do with what dogs are, spiritually speaking. In theory, other wild canids wouldn't be a problem. A good example would be Garou breeding with Dingos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T09:39:27-07:00","id":675321,"title":"","content":"I think a restriction on Pure Breed, being both spirit and physical, might be an option. The eastern coyote wolf hybrids are at least from what I've read taking the place of the red wolf. I know that there is some concern that the red wolf might be replaced completely. Of course at least one scientist has suggested that the hybrids are exactly how the red wolf originally evolved. I have not read any scientific journal article, but the blurbs and summaries make for interesting reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T12:54:27-07:00","id":676734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/555110-how-would-you-handle-species-hybridization-in-game?p=556222#post556222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My player who has an environmental science degree said that the black fur color that pops up sometimes in coyotes has been traced to wolves, which then was traced back to dogs....anyone know anything about this? Could be fun at the Shadow Lord and Black Furies expense!</div> </div> </div> </div>It is thought that the mutation for black fur did arise in dogs but the timeframe ranges from 12k to 121k years ago. I'd think that that many years would allow the wolves to remain more or less &quot;spiritually pure&quot; to breed with and produce Garou, though the funny aspect of black colored European Garou tribes is that black wolves are much more common in North America and are a rare occurrence in European populations of wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}